<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  PROBE B1. What this asks: can a boxed CONTEXT entry (a section 4.4 hydrator
  entry) INVOKE a business knowledge model?

  This is the highest consequence question in the Phase 5 matrix. Phase 3.6
  already ships hydrators, Phase 5 ships BKMs, and every record with a computed
  field that calls a tier 2 decide is exactly this shape. A Camunda 8 failure
  here kills the corpus at the DEFAULT flavor, not at an opt in.

  Shape:

      decision `investor` = boxed context
          annual_income : investor_raw.annual_income   (plain projection)
          net_worth     : investor_raw.net_worth       (plain projection)
          grade         : classify(investor_raw.annual_income)   <<< BKM CALL
      decision `eligible` = investor.grade = "A"

  DELIBERATELY DISTINCT from PR #176's spouse-context-table.dmn, which put a
  decisionTable (a tFunctionDefinition) INSIDE the context entry and which
  Camunda 8 rejected at parse with `expected literal expression but found
  '...DecisionTableImpl...'`. Here the entry IS a literalExpression, and the
  table, if any, lives inside the BKM where DMN puts it. Only NAME RESOLUTION
  across the context boundary is in question: does a BKM name declared by a
  knowledgeRequirement on the ENCLOSING decision reach into the context body?

  WHAT A FLIP MEANS. If either engine cannot resolve the BKM from inside the
  context, hydrators and BKMs cannot compose, and the emitter must either (a)
  un-hydrate any record with a calling computed field back into separate
  decisions, or (b) inline the BKM body at every call site, defeating the whole
  point of Phase 5. Both are large, and the choice would be forced by this one
  measurement.

  MEASURED 2026-07-31: 6/6 values on BOTH engines, KIE clean, Camunda clean.
  The highest-consequence unknown in the Phase 5 matrix resolves favourably: a
  boxed context entry MAY invoke a BKM declared by a knowledgeRequirement on the
  enclosing decision, on the default flavor as well as on kie. Hydration and
  Phase 5 compose, and no un-hydration or inlining fallback is needed.

-->
<definitions xmlns="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/MODEL/" id="definitions_bkm_in_context" name="bkm_in_context" namespace="https://legalese.com/l4/dmn/bkm_in_context" exporter="hand">
  <itemDefinition id="itemdef_investor_raw" name="InvestorRaw">
    <itemComponent id="itemdef_investor_raw_c1" name="annual_income">
      <typeRef>number</typeRef>
    </itemComponent>
    <itemComponent id="itemdef_investor_raw_c2" name="net_worth">
      <typeRef>number</typeRef>
    </itemComponent>
  </itemDefinition>
  <itemDefinition id="itemdef_investor" name="Investor">
    <itemComponent id="itemdef_investor_c1" name="annual_income">
      <typeRef>number</typeRef>
    </itemComponent>
    <itemComponent id="itemdef_investor_c2" name="net_worth">
      <typeRef>number</typeRef>
    </itemComponent>
    <itemComponent id="itemdef_investor_c3" name="grade">
      <typeRef>string</typeRef>
    </itemComponent>
  </itemDefinition>
  <businessKnowledgeModel id="bkm_classify" name="classify">
    <variable id="bkm_classify_var" name="classify" typeRef="string"/>
    <encapsulatedLogic id="bkm_classify_logic">
      <formalParameter id="bkm_classify_p1" name="income" typeRef="number"/>
      <literalExpression id="bkm_classify_lit">
        <text>if income &gt;= 200000 then "A" else (if income &gt;= 100000 then "B" else "C")</text>
      </literalExpression>
    </encapsulatedLogic>
  </businessKnowledgeModel>
  <inputData id="input_investor_raw" name="investor_raw">
    <variable id="input_investor_raw_var" name="investor_raw" typeRef="InvestorRaw"/>
  </inputData>
  <decision id="decision_investor" name="investor" label="investor (hydrated, calls a BKM)">
    <variable id="decision_investor_var" name="investor" typeRef="Investor"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_investor_raw">
      <requiredInput href="#input_investor_raw"/>
    </informationRequirement>
    <knowledgeRequirement id="kr_investor_classify">
      <requiredKnowledge href="#bkm_classify"/>
    </knowledgeRequirement>
    <context id="ctx_investor">
      <contextEntry id="ce_annual_income">
        <variable id="ce_annual_income_var" name="annual_income" typeRef="number"/>
        <literalExpression id="ce_annual_income_lit">
          <text>investor_raw.annual_income</text>
        </literalExpression>
      </contextEntry>
      <contextEntry id="ce_net_worth">
        <variable id="ce_net_worth_var" name="net_worth" typeRef="number"/>
        <literalExpression id="ce_net_worth_lit">
          <text>investor_raw.net_worth</text>
        </literalExpression>
      </contextEntry>
      <contextEntry id="ce_grade">
        <variable id="ce_grade_var" name="grade" typeRef="string"/>
        <literalExpression id="ce_grade_lit">
          <text>classify(investor_raw.annual_income)</text>
        </literalExpression>
      </contextEntry>
    </context>
  </decision>
  <decision id="decision_eligible" name="eligible">
    <variable id="decision_eligible_var" name="eligible" typeRef="boolean"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_investor">
      <requiredDecision href="#decision_investor"/>
    </informationRequirement>
    <literalExpression id="decision_eligible_lit">
      <text>investor.grade = "A"</text>
    </literalExpression>
  </decision>
</definitions>
